==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*10 [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jrs]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Koronium]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'boin]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*6 [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'boin]] spawns after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage's challenge lies in killing Koronium despite his own waves and the powerful attacks of his supporters get in the way. This challenge can be completely avoided in two ways, which you should exploit if you can:

*Wait for Koronium to be alone in the front with no cats alive, summon [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]], or [[Million-Dollar Cat (Special Cat)|Million-Dollar Cat]], or [[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Sunny Neneko]] if you have them. Afterwards, activate a high level [[Ototo Corps|Slow Beam]]. The cannon will slow Koronium long enough to let Waitress complete her animation and just kill it while nothing else can get in the way.
*Wait for something else to be in the front and use it to trigger an attack with [[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]], which will kill Koronium from a distance.

If you can't, use regular [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|critical hitters]] and/or [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]] to sneak a hit in while others block his advance and the waves.

For the rest, you'll need tanky meatshields and/or high DPS units to kill the Bore Jr. as quickly as possible. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] will be useful, as they both outrange Bore Jr. and can hit him before they get hit.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] with a [[Special Abilities|Special Ability]] against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies and/or can do [[Critical Hit]]s with a decent chance, will be good here. Ranged [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] will also be extremely helpful here. Below are more specified examples of good [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] to use in this stage.
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]: Can destroy Koronium in this stage easily with his powerful, [[Long Distance]] strikes.
*[[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sakura Sonic]]: Great [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] for the Koronium here and has a chance to do a [[Critical Hit]].
*[[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]]: Makes Koronium a a non-threat, by killing him near instantly as long as he attacks once.
*[[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-00]]: A good ranged wave blocker for this stage, beware of his two knockbacks though, as Le'boin could be a threat to him due to Le'boin's range.
*[[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo]]: Same as EVA Unit-00, just has three knockbacks instead of two which increases her survivability.
*[[Mighty Kristul Muu (Legend Rare Cat)|Mighty Kristul Muu]]: Same as EVA Unit-00, except has one less knockback and much slower movement speed at the pro of having more range.

